{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The ranks of prophecy are many and there is no way to enumerate them, for the capacity of the souls that receive the power of the spirit of holiness to prophesy is not on a single path. And when the Glory was with Israel before they were exiled, there was no need to explain the prophecy, such as: 'Behold, a son is born to the house of David, Josiah his name' — and the matter would clarify itself. But after the exile they are visions and require interpretation, like the visions of Daniel, for had the angel not interpreted them, Daniel would not have known them, let alone others. So too the visions of Zechariah — and what the angel speaking in me interpreted, for night visions that are known and were not interpreted are sealed and hidden from the eyes of the discerning. And if we were to find an ancient book that would recount what transpired in those days of wars, we would grope like the blind at a wall to say: perhaps on account of this was the prophecy. But now we have nothing on which to lean. And I have seen the books of sages that were in France, which interpreted the visions that Zechariah saw retrospectively, concerning matters that had already passed in the days of this prophet — like the ephah, for on its account Judah was exiled to Babylon — and the two staffs they interpreted as Israel and Judah. But Scripture says: 'Feed the flock of slaughter,' and behold, the prophecy was for the future, in the days of the prophet. And now I begin to interpret:" "<b>In the month, saying</b> — to Israel; but the correct reading is: to the prophet."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved 'ספרי חכמים שהיה בצרפת' as 'the books of sages that were in France'; Ibn Ezra refers to contemporary or near-contemporary French rabbinic exegetes."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:39.065416944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}